# Phase 18 Producer fault-array nullability closure — 2026-10-14T00:48:29Z

- Continued on `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate` from `1ced0a32`. Compared the runtime Producer fault-array behavior with pinned RocketMQ Java client 5.5.1 source commit `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`. The Java checkout at `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/3rd/rocketmq` was read-only and unchanged.
- Added invoked Java fixture cases for null `latencyMax` and `notAvailableDuration` setters/getters, deferred null-pointer failures when each null table is read, an array-index failure only when a matching latency threshold reaches a missing duration row, and ignored extra duration rows. The first fixture compile needed the missing `InvocationTargetException` import; after adding it, fixture generation and drift verification passed.
- Rust `ProducerLongArray` now represents Java null separately from an empty array and exposes nullable snapshots. Fault updates return the matching Java exception class through `ProducerError`; latency-fault-disabled sends do not read the tables. Added differential assertions for null handle operations and all invoked exception/array-length branches.
- Updated `fixtures/producer/core.json`; SHA-256: `2f8c6d40c4669a6a662085e8cddef749338c91fcbb1bf64829ef1f59f77a284e`.
- Code, oracle, and fixture were committed as `1845c55a` (`fix(producer): preserve nullable fault tables`). Phase 7 Producer matrix, Phase 6 audit, release checklist, and this log are being recorded separately.

